Looks: a pack the owner added is plain to find and wear, and a downloaded
PNGtuber (a .zip or its PNGs) becomes a character any agent can wear.

Adding a pack in the Shop put it in the wardrobe, but the customizer only
un-dimmed its pieces among the starter's across seven layer tabs, so it
looked as if nothing had arrived. Now the Shop says where it went, with a
"Wear it on Looks" button; the Looks gallery names what is in the wardrobe;
the customizer has a "Your packs" card with each added pack's sheet and a
"Wear it" button that puts the pack's pieces on in one tap.

A PNGtuber from the store downloads as a zip of frames (01_closed, 02_open,
03_closed_blink, reactions). The customizer's Characters card imports one:
the zip is read in the browser, the closed, open and blink frames are picked
by name, each is fitted under the gateway's 64 KB body limit and sent to the
Runtime, which keeps it in <install root>/looks/characters/<id>/ for every
agent. A look may name a character (`character`): the dashboard then draws
the character's frames, talking and blinking like the pixel ones, over the
parts, which stay as the fallback (and what the agent's own look tool edits).

The overlay holds the gateway routes' handlers (api_looks.rs), the client
(lib/characters.ts), the logic (looks/characters.logic.ts, its tests in
looks.logic.test.ts), the renderer (looks/Look.tsx) and the pages
(pages/Looks.tsx, pages/Shop.tsx); this patch routes /api/looks/characters
(lib.rs) and adds the strings (i18n.ts).

--- a/crates/caelza-gateway/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/caelza-gateway/src/lib.rs
@@ -2412,6 +2412,16 @@ pub async fn run_gateway_with_plugin_webhooks(
             get(api_looks::handle_wardrobe_get).put(api_looks::handle_wardrobe_put),
         )
         .route("/api/looks/wardrobe/unlock", post(api_looks::handle_wardrobe_unlock))
+        // The drawn characters the owner imported (a PNGtuber's frames), wearable by any agent.
+        .route("/api/looks/characters", get(api_looks::handle_characters_list))
+        .route(
+            "/api/looks/characters/{id}",
+            put(api_looks::handle_character_put).delete(api_looks::handle_character_delete),
+        )
+        .route(
+            "/api/looks/characters/{id}/{frame}",
+            get(api_looks::handle_character_frame_get).put(api_looks::handle_character_frame_put),
+        )
         // The voice (vision M10 §10): what the agent sounds like when a device
         // reads its replies aloud; the devices' offers; the owner's ElevenLabs voices.
         .route(
